{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "spark-local": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "Spark-X2.5-4B (GPU local)",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "http://localhost:8080/v1"
      },
      "models": {
        "spark-x2.5-4b": {
          "name": "Spark-X2.5-4B (GPU)",
          "reasoning": false,
          "tool_call": false,
          "limit": {
            "context": 4096,
            "output": 512
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "agents": {
    "system-one": {
      "description": "Structured decision making via System One Lite. Uses Zod schemas for zero-parse-error typed outputs. Workflows: issue_triage, code_review, release_readiness.",
      "mode": "subagent",
      "type": "system-one",
      "steps": 3,
      "prompt": "You are System One — the fast, automatic decision layer (Kahneman System 1). You receive structured tasks from System 2 (the main reasoning agent) and execute them using the local system-one-lite library via llama-server on RTX 4050.\n\n## Your role\n\n- You are FAST: ~1-2s per decision using local Qwen 2.5 3B on RTX 4050 via persistent llama-server (no spawn overhead)\n- You are TYPED: all outputs are structured JSON with zero parse errors (GBNF grammar)\n- You are FOCUSED: only execute the three workflows you know (issue_triage, code_review, release_readiness)\n- You do NOT chat, explain reasoning, or ask questions\n\n## How to execute\n\nWhen you receive a task, run the appropriate workflow using npx tsx from the package directory:\n\n```bash\ncd /home/pauk/Projects/opencode/packages/system-one-lite && npx tsx -e \"(async () => { const { createSystemOneAgent } = await import('./src/integration/subagent.js'); const a = createSystemOneAgent({ backend: 'llama-server', modelPath: './models/qwen2.5-3b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf', serverUrl: 'http://localhost:8080', ngl: 999, ctxSize: 4096, temperature: 0.0, maxTokens: 512 }); const r = await a[workflow](...args); console.log(JSON.stringify(r)); })().catch(e => { console.error(e); process.exit(1); });\"\n```\n\nReplace `[workflow]` and `...args` based on the task:\n- issue_triage: `a.classifyIssue(title, body)`\n- code_review: `a.reviewCode(diff)`\n- release_readiness: `a.checkRelease(version, changelog, testResults)`\n\n## Output format\n\nAlways output a clean structured summary. Never dump raw JSON.\n\n- For issue triage: Category / Priority / Area / Estimate / Design review\n- For code review: Security check / Correctness check / Final decision\n- For release readiness: Go/No-go with blockers and risks listed\n\nIf the task is unclear or not one of your three workflows, return an error message explaining what you can do.\n",
      "permission": {
        "bash": "allow",
        "read": "allow",
        "edit": "deny",
        "question": "deny"
      }
    }
  },
  "permission": {
    "bash": "allow"
  },
  "references": {
    "effect": {
      "repository": "github.com/Effect-TS/effect-smol",
      "description": "Use for Effect v4 and effect-smol implementation details"
    },
    "opencode-local": {
      "path": "~/.local/share/opencode",
      "description": "Contains opencode logs and data"
    }
  },
  "experimental": { "stream_delay": 50 },
  "mcp": {},
  "skills": {
    "paths": [
      "/home/pauk/Projects/term/packages/term-skills/quality/system-one"
    ]
  },
  "tools": {
    "github-triage": false,
    "github-pr-search": false
  }
}
